4. Root Causes of Failure
CAUSE 1: Tailwind Version Collision (Styling Loss)
The root app uses Tailwind CSS v3 (PostCSS-based, @tailwind base/components/utilities directives).
The landing page uses Tailwind CSS v4 (Vite plugin-based, @layer base/@layer components with CSS-native syntax, oklch colors).
Line 1 of c:\...\styles.css does @import "./landing-page/src/styles.css", pulling the landing page's v4 CSS into the root app's v3 PostCSS pipeline.
Tailwind v4's @layer directives and oklch custom properties are processed by v3's PostCSS plugin, which does not understand them. This causes unpredictable cascade ordering, lost utility classes, and broken custom properties -- the exact "styling loss" reported.
CAUSE 2: Cross-Boundary Component Import (Navigation Breaks)
Line 12 of c:\...\pycademy-python-learning-platform.jsx does:
import { LandingPage as PublicLandingPage } from "./landing-page/src/routes/index.tsx";
This imports a TanStack Router route component (which uses createFileRoute) directly into the root app's plain React tree. The component depends on:
TanStack Router context (Route.useRouteContext() in __root.tsx)
The Button component from shadcn/ui (which uses class-variance-authority, @radix-ui/react-slot)
Tailwind v4 utility classes
The root app has none of these dependencies installed. The import works only because Vite resolves it from the landing-page/node_modules directory at dev time, creating a fragile cross-boundary resolution. In production builds, this fails because:
The root vite.config.js has no React plugin configured (line 1-6 show only base is set)
TSX files from the landing page cannot be transpiled without the TypeScript/React plugin
Dependencies like class-variance-authority, @radix-ui/react-slot, cmdk, etc. are not in the root node_modules
CAUSE 3: Missing Vite React Plugin in Root Config
c:\...\vite.config.js contains only base: '/PyCademy/'. It does not import or configure @vitejs/plugin-react. Despite having the plugin as a dependency, it is never activated. This means JSX transform relies on implicit/default behavior, and TSX imports from the landing page are not handled.
CAUSE 4: The Navigation Model is Incompatible
The landing page's LandingPage component accepts onLogin and onSignup callbacks (line 258 of index.tsx).
The root app wires these (lines 9599-9601) to toggle showLanding state and switch to AuthScreen.
The landing page's own "Create Account" and "Log In" buttons in the hero section (lines 356-361) do not use onLogin/onSignup -- they call scrollTo("final") as a fallback. Only the nav-bar buttons (lines 322-323) and mobile menu buttons (lines 336-337) properly use the callbacks.
When navigation "stopped working," it was likely because the build started failing on the cross-boundary TSX import, producing a broken bundle.
CAUSE 5: Deploy Workflow Builds Root App Only
c:\...\.github\workflows\deploy.yml runs npm ci and npm run build at the repository root.
This builds only the root Vite app. The landing-page's TanStack Start/Nitro SSR build is never executed in CI.
The dist/ directory is empty, confirming builds are not succeeding or not being run locally either.
